==German==

===Etymology===
From {{etyl|gmh|de}} {{term|obez|lang=gmh}}, from {{etyl|goh|de}} {{term|obez|lang=goh}}, {{term|obaz||fruit|lang=goh}}, from {{etyl|gem-pro|de}} {{m|gem-pro|*ubatją||fruit, produce, increase}}, from a compound whose first element represents {{etyl|ine-pro|de}} {{m|ine-pro|*obʰi-}}, {{m|ine-pro|*ebʰi-}}, {{m|ine-pro|*bʰi-||on, toward, from, by}}, and whose second element is {{etyl|gem-pro|de}} {{m|gem-pro|*at}}, {{m|gem-pro|*ēta-||edibles, food}}, from {{etyl|gem-pro|de}} {{m|gem-pro|*etaną||to eat}}, from {{etyl|ine-pro|de}} {{m|ine-pro|*h₁ed-||to eat}}. Cognate with {{etyl|en|-}} {{term|ovest||mast|lang=en}}, {{etyl|gml|-}} {{term|ōvet|lang=gml}}, {{term|āvet|lang=gml}}, {{term|ōft||fruit|lang=gml}}, {{etyl|nds|-}} {{term|Aavt||fruits|lang=nds-de}}, {{etyl|nl|-}} {{term|ooft||fruits|lang=nl}}. More at {{l|en|ovest}}.

===Pronunciation===
*{{IPA|lang=de|/oːpst/}}
* {{audio|De-Obst.ogg|audio|lang=de}}

===Noun===
{{de-noun|n|Obstes|gen2=Obsts|-}}

# [[fruit]]
#: ''Heute esse ich nur '''Obst'''.'' - Today I only eat fruit.

